@import '../../styles/tokens.styl'

// THE ONE ROW THAT IS NOT ONE LINE, and the exception is the point of the rest.
//
// Every other entry in the expanded list is clamped to a line, so what the
// agent SAID is the only thing on the surface allowed to run to its natural
// length — it is the run's own account of itself, and a reader scanning a
// hundred rows of tool traffic is looking for exactly these. Full ink against
// the muted rows around it and a little air above and below is the whole of the
// emphasis; no ground, no rule, no box.
//
// NO LABEL AND THEREFORE NO LABEL COLUMN, which is the second half of the same
// emphasis. Wearing the word ASSISTANT the row said again what its shape
// already showed; without it the row also sheds the fixed indent every other
// row keeps in order to line its body up, so the message starts at the same
// left edge the panel does. That flush edge, against the indented one-line rows
// above and below, is what says "this is the agent talking".
//
// A measure, because this is the only prose on the surface and prose set to the
// full width of a share page is a line nobody can track back from. The same
// 68ch the consuming page gives its own paragraphs.
//
// Scoped to the expanded list. Collapsed, the panel shows one row that changes
// on every live entry, and an assistant message allowed to wrap there would
// make the host panel as tall as whatever the agent last said and jump on every
// tick — which is the failure the collapsed clamp exists to prevent.
.rat-timeline-expanded .rat-event-row-assistant-message .rat-event-body
  white-space pre-wrap
  overflow visible
  text-overflow clip
  color $rat_text
  line-height 1.5
  max-width 68ch

.rat-timeline-expanded .rat-event-row-assistant-message .rat-event-row-main
  padding-top $rat_space
  padding-bottom $rat_space
